===Etymology===
From {{der|en|xno|receptacle}}, from {{der|en|frm|receptacle||[[organ]] [[contain]]ing a [[fluid]]; [[gather]]ing [[place]]; [[water]] [[basin]]}} (modern {{cog|fr|réceptacle}}), from {{der|en|la|receptāculum||[[animal]] [[enclosure]], [[container]], place of [[refuge]], receptacle, [[repository]], [[reservoir]], [[shelter#Noun|shelter]]}}, from {{m|la|receptāre||to [[harbour#Verb|harbour]], to [[receive]], to [[shelter#Verb|shelter]]}} or {{m|la|receptō||I receive [[back#Adverb|back]] or [[again]], I [[recover]]}}, [[frequentative]] of {{m|la|recipiō||I receive; I [[hold back]], I [[reserve#Verb|reserve]]}} (from {{m|la|re-||back, again}} + {{m|la|capiō||I [[hold#Verb|hold]]}}) + {{m|la|-culum||''suffix forming nouns from verbs, particularly nouns representing [[tool#Noun|tools]] and [[instrument]]s''}}; cognate with {{cog|it|recettaculo}}, {{m|it|ricettaculo}}, {{cog|pt|receptáculo}}, {{cog|es|receptáculo}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ɹɪˈsɛptəkl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ɹəˈsɛptək(ə)l/|/ɹi-/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|re|cep|ta|cle|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[container]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} The part of the [[flower]] [[stalk]] ([[peduncle]] or [[pedicel]]) to which the [[floral]] parts are [[attach#Verb|attached]]; the [[torus]].
## In the ''[[Asteraceae]]'', the end of the peduncle to which all of the [[floret]]s of the [[flower head]] are attached.
# {{lb|en|electricity|US}} A [[contact]] [[device]] [[install]]ed at an [[outlet]] for the [[connection]] of an [[attachment]] [[plug#Noun|plug]] and [[flexible]] [[cord]] to [[supply#Verb|supply]] [[portable]] [[appliance]]s or [[equipment]].

